    {
     "t": "heading",
     "pg": 158,
     "level": 3,
     "s": "NIGHT. STREET BEFORE MARGARET’S DOOR"
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 158,
     "s": "Valentine (a soldier, Margaret’s brother)"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 158,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "When seated ’mong the jovial crowd,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Where merry comrades boasting loud",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Each named with pride his favourite lass,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And in her honour drain’d his glass;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Upon my elbows I would lean,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "With easy quiet view the scene,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Nor give my tongue the rein until",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Each swaggering blade had talked his fill.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Then smiling I my beard would stroke,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The while, with brimming glass, I spoke;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "“Each to his taste!—but to my mind,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Where in the country will you find,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "A maid, as my dear Gretchen fair,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Who with my sister can compare?”",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Cling! Clang! so rang the jovial sound!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Shouts of assent went circling round;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Pride of her sex is she!—cried some;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Then were the noisy boasters dumb.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 159,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And now!—I could tear out my hair,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Or dash my brains out in despair!—",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Me every scurvy knave may twit,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "With stinging jest and taunting sneer!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Like skulking debtor I must sit,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And sweat each casual word to hear!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And though I smash’d them one and all,—",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Yet them I could not liars call.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 159,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Who comes this way? who’s sneaking here?",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "If I mistake not, two draw near.",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "If he be one, have at him;—well I wot",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Alive he shall not leave this spot!",
       "i": 2
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 159,
     "s": "FAUST. MEPHISTOPHELES"
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 159,
     "s": "Faust"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 159,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "How from yon sacristy, athwart the night,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Its beams the ever-burning taper throws,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "While ever waning, fades the glimmering light,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "As gathering darkness doth around it close!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "So night-like gloom doth in my bosom reign.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 159,
     "s": "Mephistopheles"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 159,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "I’m like a tom-cat in a thievish vein,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "That up fire-ladders tall and steep,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "And round the walls doth slyly creep;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Virtuous withal, I feel, with, I confess,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "A touch of thievish joy and wantonness.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Thus through my limbs already burns",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "The glorious Walpurgis night!",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "After to-morrow it returns,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Then why one wakes, one knows aright!",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 160,
     "s": "Faust"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 160,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Meanwhile, the treasure I see glimmering there,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Will it ascend into the open air?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 160,
     "s": "Mephistopheles"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 160,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Ere long thou wilt proceed with pleasure,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "To raise the casket with its treasure;",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I took a peep, therein are stored,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Of lion-dollars a rich hoard.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 160,
     "s": "Faust"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 160,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "And not a trinket? not a ring?",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Wherewith my lovely girl to deck?",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 160,
     "s": "Mephistopheles"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 160,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "I saw among them some such thing,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "A string of pearls to grace her neck.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 160,
     "s": "Faust"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 160,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "’Tis well! I’m always loath to go,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Without some gift my love to show.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "speaker",
     "pg": 160,
     "s": "Mephistopheles"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 160,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Some pleasures gratis to enjoy,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "Should surely cause you no annoy.",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "While bright with stars the heavens appear,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "I’ll sing a masterpiece of art:",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "A moral song shall charm her ear,",
       "i": 0
      },
      {
       "s": "More surely to beguile her heart.",
       "i": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "stage",
     "pg": 161,
     "s": "(Sings to the guitar.)"
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 161,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Kathrina say,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Why lingering stay",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "At dawn of day",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Before your lover’s door?",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Maiden, beware,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Nor enter there,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Lest forth you fare,",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "A maiden never more.",
       "i": 2
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "t": "verse",
     "pg": 161,
     "lines": [
      {
       "s": "Maiden take heed!",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Reck well my rede!",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Is’t done, the deed?",
       "i": 2
      },
      {
       "s": "Good night, you poor, poor thing!",
